vardct: reject varblocks larger than 8x8 in a frame with chroma subsampling, as libjxl does
(DecodeAcMetadata: "AC strategy not compatible with chroma subsampling"). The HF coefficients of a
subsampled channel are decoded with the varblock size found at the subsampled position, so a large
varblock there reached past the channel's grids (hf_coeff.rs: index out of bounds in the non-zeros
grid; mutable_subgrid.rs: row index out of range). Channel
shifts are compared as libjxl does, relative to the largest sampling factor, so a frame whose
channels all share one sampling factor counts as 4:4:4. Test: varblock_chroma_subsampling
(crates/jxl-oxide-tests/tests/varblock_chroma_subsampling.rs).

Upstream: not reported; the code is unchanged at upstream HEAD (c0cc4c7, 2026-08-15). Open PR #510
(apply CfL when all channels share the sampling) fixes the same 4:4:4 test in render_vardct and
JpegBitstreamReconstructor; this check already uses ChannelShift, which compares the same way.

